{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Ktu9ehi1rb9PUtR9HV7LiJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is an experiment in specification-driven development. It derives formal specs from C source code, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity against GNU reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go implementations), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (platform syscall abstraction), `pkg/format/` (shared formatting), `magefiles/` (build infrastructure, scaffolded).\n\n**Current state**: Source code exists for `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, `cmd/cat` (main + test), `cmd/du` (main + test), `cmd/sponge` (main + test), and `cmd/wc` (main only — no test file in source). Releases 00.0, 01.1, 01.2, 01.3 are effectively complete in source. Releases 02.0–02.2 have pending specs (human-authored, not a generation target). Release 03.0 (wc) has spec complete and implementation exists but differential tests are missing. Releases 04.0/04.1 (ls) have specs complete but no code.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nThe earliest incomplete release with actionable code work is **03.0 (wc)**. `cmd/wc/main.go` exists but `cmd/wc/wc_test.go` is absent — every other `cmd/` package has both. Per P5, tests come before further implementation. This unblocks marking rel03.0-uc001-wc as code-complete and validates the existing wc implementation against the GNU reference binary before moving to ls (04.0).\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/wc differential tests -- prd005-wc R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - cmd/wc/main.go (existing wc implementation covering flags, counting, output formatting)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests, NormalizeFunc API)\n      - cmd/cat/cat_test.go (reference pattern for TestMain, writeTestFile, normalizeProgramName, and differential test structure)\n      - cmd/du/du_test.go (reference pattern for multi-case differential testing)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd005-wc.yaml (full PRD for wc utility)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-03.0.yaml (test suite specification for wc)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/wc/wc_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for wc against GNU gwc reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement differential tests verifying prd005-wc R1.1: default mode (no flags) counts lines, words, and bytes for a single file, and individual flag selection (-l, -w, -c) each produce output matching gwc byte-for-byte\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement differential tests verifying prd005-wc R1.2: wc reads from stdin when no file arguments are given and when '-' appears as a file argument, matching gwc output\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement differential tests verifying prd005-wc R1.3: each output line has right-justified counts with column widths matching gwc, followed by the filename\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement differential tests verifying prd005-wc R1.4: when two or more files are given, wc prints a 'total' summary line after the per-file lines, matching gwc\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the established TestMain pattern: build the Go wc binary into a temp directory via 'go build -o goBinary .', locate the GNU reference binary via exec.LookPath('gwc'), and skip all tests with os.Exit(0) if gwc is not on PATH. Clean up the temp binary directory after m.Run().\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use testutils.RunDiffTests with DiffTest structs for all test cases. Compare stdout, stderr, and exit code between the Go binary and gwc. Set ExitCode in each DiffTest to the expected value.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Include a normalizeProgramName function that replaces 'gwc: ' with 'wc: ' in stderr output, following the pattern in cmd/cat/cat_test.go. Use this in the Normalize field of DiffTest for error-path tests.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Create test input files using a writeTestFile helper (same signature as cmd/cat/cat_test.go). Use t.TempDir() for per-test isolation. Mark all top-level test functions with t.Parallel().\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/wc/wc_test.go compiles without errors as part of the cmd/wc package\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"'go test ./cmd/wc/' passes when gwc is available on PATH\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"At least one test verifies single-file default-mode counting (lines, words, bytes)\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"At least one test verifies stdin-no-args and stdin-dash-arg modes\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"At least one test verifies the total line appears for multi-file invocations\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"All test functions use testutils.RunDiffTests for byte-for-byte comparison against gwc\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":68207,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":68207},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"39795f43-b454-49f1-8317-164538adf928","uuid":"0792e45d-b449-4603-acdc-2d1057ef1c75"}
